      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-02-07T20:54:52.000Z",
      "title": "Dividend increased to ₹12.70",
      "body": "Dividend of ₹12.70 is 49% higher than last year. Ex-date: 11th February 2026 Payment date: 7th March 2026 Dividend yield will be 1.1%, which is higher than the industry average of 0.8%. Sustainability & Growth Dividend is well covered by both earnings (14% earnings payout ratio) and cash flows (32% cash payout ratio). The dividend has increased by an average of 23% per year over the past 10 years. However, payments have been volatile during that time. EPS is expected to grow by 40% over the next 2 years, which should provide support to the dividend and adequate earnings cover.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "d8d3d9d2-e9d1-4015-9886-fd01e970c934",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-02-03T00:00:00.000Z",
      "title": "Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited (BSE:500420) completed the acquisition of 2.8% stake in J. B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals Limited (BSE:506943) from certain employees.",
      "body": "Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited (BSE:500420) proposed to acquire 2.8% stake in J. B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals Limited (BSE:506943) from certain employees for INR 7.2 billion on June 29, 2025. Torrent Pharmaceuticals signed a share purchase agreement to acquire 2.8% stake in J. B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals from certain employees for INR 6.2 billion on July 3, 2025. A cash consideration valued at INR 1600 per share will be paid by Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited. In related transactions, Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited will acquire up to 41.7 million shares at INR 1,639.18 per share via open offer, and 46.39% stake in J. B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals from KKR Asian Fund III, managed by KKR & Co for approximately INR 120 billion. Torrent Pharmaceuticals has authorized its representative",
      "keyDevTypeId": "81",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "71115524-3f87-4d3b-857c-1167fef5eb39",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-02-01T17:44:03.000Z",
      "title": "High number of new and inexperienced directors",
      "body": "There are 7 new directors who have joined the board in the last 3 years. The company's board is composed of: 7 new directors. 2 experienced directors. No highly experienced directors. Non-Executive & Independent Director Sumit Bose is the most experienced director on the board, commencing their role in 2020. The following issues are considered to be risks according to the Simply Wall St Risk Model: Lack of board continuity. Lack of experienced directors.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "33f30d5d-2493-4e89-9f83-4b7db5386ee0",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-01-21T09:02:00.000Z",
      "title": "J.B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals Limited Announces Resignation of Nikhil Chopra as CEO, Effective from March 31, 2026",
      "body": "J.B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals Limited announced that Mr. Nikhil Chopra has resigned as Chief Executive Officer. His resignation as Whole-time Director and as a member of any committees of the Board will be effective upon the conclusion of the Board meeting held on January 21, 2026, and his resignation as CEO of the Company shall be effective from March 31, 2026. Mr. Nikhil Chopra is resigning on account of personal reasons and to pursue other professional opportunities.",
      "keyDevTypeId": "101",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "8ac1d8dd-34b6-4e4e-a7e0-bcfde31aef0c",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-01-21T09:02:00.000Z",
      "title": "J.B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals Limited Announces Resignation of Non-Executive Directors and Committee Changes, Effective January 21, 2026",
      "body": "J.B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals Limited announced the resignation of Mr. Gaurav Trehan, Mr. Akshay Tanna, and Mr. Prashant Kumar, all non-executive non-independent directors of the Company, as directors from the Board with effect from conclusion of the board meeting held on January 21, 2026. The resignations are due to change in control of the Company as per the share purchase agreement dated June 29, 2025 executed between Tau Investment Holdings Pte. Ltd., Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited, and the Company, read with the addendum dated July 3, 2025, and to facilitate the reconstitution of the board of directors of the Company. The Board also took on record the resignation letter(s) received from each of Mr. Gaurav Trehan, Mr. Akshay Tanna and Mr. Prashant Kumar. The Board has also taken on",
      "keyDevTypeId": "16",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "973598a7-78e3-42ef-b910-9e5386249ea2",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-01-21T00:00:00.000Z",
      "title": "Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited (BSE:500420) completed the acquisition of 46.39% stake in J. B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals Limited (BSE:506943) from KKR Asian Fund III, managed by KKR & Co. Inc. (NYSE:KKR).",
      "body": "Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited (BSE:500420) agreed to acquire 46.39% stake in J. B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals Limited (BSE:506943) from KKR Asian Fund III, managed by KKR & Co. Inc. (NYSE:KKR) for approximately INR 120 billion on June 29, 2025. A cash consideration valued at INR 1600 per share will be paid by Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited. As per the transaction, Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited will acquire 74.5 million shares of J. B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals Limited. In related transactions, Torrent Pharmaceuticals Limited will acquire upto 41.7 million shares at INR 1,639.18 per share via open offer, 4.5 million shares of J. B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals Limited at INR 1600 per share from certain employees of J. B. Chemicals & Pharmaceuticals Limited. Also their will be a merge",
      "keyDevTypeId": "81",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "467190c5-b737-492d-b210-86b41f8e49aa",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-01-20T11:46:39.000Z",
      "title": "Third quarter 2026 earnings: Revenues and EPS in line with analyst expectations",
      "body": "Third quarter 2026 results: EPS: ₹12.63 (up from ₹10.46 in 3Q 2025). Revenue: ₹10.6b (up 11% from 3Q 2025). Net income: ₹1.98b (up 22% from 3Q 2025). Profit margin: 19% (up from 17% in 3Q 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue was in line with analyst estimates. Earnings per share (EPS) were also in line with analyst expectations. Revenue is forecast to grow 12% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 10% growth forecast for the Pharmaceuticals industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 20% per year whereas the company’s share price has increased by 24% per year.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "22749c88-231e-493f-8b18-bce9300c2ce5",
